# Prahari — local secrets and model choices.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory (the project root) and fill in
# the key. `.env` is git-ignored; this example is the only version committed.
#
# The provider is detected from the key itself:
#   sk-or-...    OpenRouter  — one key, many models (recommended)
#   sk-ant-...   Anthropic direct
#
# Nothing else is required. Without a key the compiler, every analysis and the
# IDE work exactly the same; only AI review is unavailable.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- models, per use case ---------------------------------------------------
#
# The defaults below need no configuration. They were chosen in three stages —
# published benchmarks, a live probe of every candidate, and
# `python eval/model_bench.py` against this project's ground truth — and
# docs/AI.md records the evidence. Free-only mode is ON for OpenRouter: any id
# that does not end in `:free` is refused before a request is made.

# Review — `prahari audit --adjudicate` and CI. Accuracy first (reasoning: medium).
# PRAHARI_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

# Interactive — "Review Findings with AI" in the IDE (reasoning: low, faster).
# PRAHARI_MODEL_INTERACTIVE=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

# Tried in order when the primary is rate-limited or down. Different providers.
# PRAHARI_MODEL_FALLBACKS=cohere/north-mini-code:free,dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free

# How much the reasoning models think: none | minimal | low | medium | high
# PRAHARI_AI_REASONING=medium
# PRAHARI_AI_REASONING_INTERACTIVE=low

# --- free-tier limits -------------------------------------------------------
#
# OpenRouter free models: 20 requests/minute, and 50/day on accounts that have
# not bought credits. Prahari paces under the per-minute limit and stops cleanly,
# with the reset time, when the daily limit is reached.

# PRAHARI_AI_RPM=16
# PRAHARI_AI_MAX_REQUESTS=200

# Refuse non-free models (on by default for OpenRouter). Set 0 only deliberately.
# PRAHARI_AI_FREE_ONLY=1

# Set to 0 to bypass the verdict cache (re-audits of unchanged code are free and
# reproducible while it is on — which matters with a daily request cap).
# PRAHARI_AI_CACHE=1
